revoked. This licence governs this version and every version after it.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   With a valid licence key, you may install and use the software to run the
   dental practice named when the key was issued, on up to the number of
   devices the key states. A licence key covers one practice, including its
   computers, phones and tablets.

   You may take and keep backups. You may keep using a version you have
   already installed for as long as your licence period runs.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   You may not copy, distribute, sell, rent, lend, sub-licence or publish the
   software, in whole or in part, to anyone else.

   You may not share, publish or resell a licence key, or use one issued to
   another practice.

   You may not remove, disable or work around the licensing in the software,
   nor help anyone else to.

   You may not remove copyright notices.

3. YOUR RECORDS ARE YOURS

   The patient records, appointments, invoices, payments and everything else
   you enter belong to you. They are stored on your own computers and phones.
   Nothing in this licence gives the copyright holder any claim to them, and
   nothing in the software sends them anywhere.

   If your licence expires or ends, the software becomes read-only: you can
   still open, search, print and export everything you have. Your records are
   never withheld from you.

4. SUPPORT AND UPDATES

   Support and updates are whatever was agreed when you bought the licence. A
   subscription (monthly or yearly) includes updates released while it runs. A
   one-off purchase includes the version sold and any updates the copyright
   holder chooses to provide.

5. NO WARRANTY

   The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability,
   fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.

   THE SOFTWARE IS NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE. It records what you type. It does not
   diagnose, and it does not check your clinical or financial decisions. You
   remain responsible for the accuracy of your records, for keeping backups,
   and for meeting the record-keeping, privacy and tax obligations that apply
   to your practice where you work.

6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

   To the fullest extent permitted by law, the copyright holder is not liable
   for any claim, damages, lost records, lost income or other liability
   arising from the software or its use. Where liability cannot be excluded,
   it is limited to the amount you paid for your licence in the twelve months
   before the claim.

7. ENDING THE LICENCE

   This licence ends if you break its terms. On ending, you must stop using
   the software; you may keep your records and your backups.

